      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-03-14T15:51:08.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"PAShortt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pashortt/48/2699_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> PAShortt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm sorry if this has been asked already, but I couldn't find an answer to this, and it's been on my mind for a while.When a Hero can choose which damage type they inflict (such as Mr Fixer, depending on his fighting style), are they allowed to choose \"irreducable\"?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Unfortunaley no. Irreducable is not a damage \"type\". It is a modifier in addition to its type and amount.</p>",
